 "version": 1,
 "note": "Emotion director table. Single source of truth for poses; the mind only knows family ids. Every ladder pose must be group a or a* in the groups sheet and live in the face catalogue (unit tests). Pip-clause lexicon: lowercase ASCII words; one word may offer alternatives with |; kinds: word (one word anywhere), phrase (consecutive words anywhere), start (words begin the clause, no leading quote), whole (the whole clause, one trailing .!? allowed). Optional row attributes: tight true (no comma between the words); after break (the match must end the clause or be followed by . , ! ? ; : or a dash or ellipsis); opener true (a weak greeting: dropped when any other row matches); refuse_next (phrases that must not follow the match directly); max_rest (at most this many words after the match). Context guards for every row: a hyphenated compound, and a one or two letter match in capitals, never match; word and phrase rows refuse a negator or hedge (not, no, never, if, would, could ...) within four tokens before them in the same sentence, a guard phrase (far from, less than, anything but) just before, and a sentence that opens with if, would, could, might, whether or in case. Rows of a family with polarity 0 or above also refuse a question (the sentence ends with ?), and a clause that carries a caution word or a negator outside the match (unless the row sets cautions false, as the comforting support rows do). All matches in a clause are collected: a contrast word anywhere, or two matches of different polarity, give no reaction; any other match beats an opener. Families may set wire_min, the lowest strength a heard cue needs.",
 "weights": {"heard": 4.0, "reply": 3.0, "event": 2.0, "job": 2.0, "tag": 0.5, "drive": 0.15},
 "holds": {"heard": 1.2, "reply": 8.0, "event": 2.0, "job": 2.5, "tag": 8.0, "drive": 1.0},
